{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-noetherian}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:566028ca14b1285b267526e091b053f96d19b314dd81659926c8191fc0f8ef3f", "source_text": "Noetherian schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5553dbb438021617de927d033d11e3a1926300736df4bca5cf44a372cf68a637", "unit_id": "tag:01OU:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:103c4d2b7eba8315df9a978e976ac0b41d8778b6af7fbee40f280209877d12d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5510dca9a502d6cccadc7a384c2b67406363f209b66da5b9933b5525b7a4435d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Noetherian<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it satisfies the ascending\nchain condition of ideals. Equivalently every ideal of <MATH_0002> is finitely\ngenerated.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6e1751100cd9f1f42d4f389efc3d04d77f5a4dd211c99130a019ea219b331908", "unit_id": "tag:01OU:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6f5cb3726ebe5a65317da64d9211d6df4f6e37cc09785bffc0682e3c40108d2d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7828eb8d35e8384108730fc7c952b9caaf1ae0544b0d8959a3b31183f314857", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>locally Noetherian<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if every\n<MATH_0003> has an affine open neighbourhood\n<MATH_0004> such that the ring <MATH_0005> is Noetherian.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>Noetherian<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0007> is locally Noetherian\nand quasi-compact.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef0b5bae9435e7423fbf2092ccb0e95a78f67778242e6ba0eaa95001a91ca38e", "unit_id": "tag:01OV:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1f8ea1b0f6d8f452ba6e1958fbb96f06c1a3b4a44802a50db446d950505d1e7a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the standard result characterizing locally Noetherian schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76736bbe6628049ce8c18ccbb541fb6189c44c9e57c013eb00b7ef01dd8e1da8", "unit_id": "tag:01OU:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-Noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2d3470cfd4ad072e56720f3c7e02d2e97fa00573f0d09f46d31f5152379bc18", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is locally Noetherian.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis Noetherian.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is Noetherian.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is locally Noetherian.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is locally Noetherian then every open subscheme\nis locally Noetherian.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57941e14b6498e5e216cddd5fbe63e4395acb447c02ba27a54c13c83423b5e65", "unit_id": "tag:01OW:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-P}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-cover}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{definition-property-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0465195623c590711849ec963252da2451c84655a1e01c19d0fceb1652670cb6", "source_text": "To show this it suffices to show that being Noetherian is a local\nproperty of rings, see Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAny localization of a Noetherian ring is Noetherian, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nBy Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003> we see the second\nproperty to Definition <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d23182a90d56fb6e7c203d6188caa5457a5e300d7fed3e30832d8fe84c82939", "unit_id": "tag:01OW:proof"}
